export const title = "Eagle Eye Networks Integration Guide";
export const html = "<h1>Eagle Eye Networks Integration Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<h2>1. Introduction</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.1 Prerequisites</h3>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>AIBridge FW version 104000 or greater.</li>\n<li>Eagle Eye Networks web version 3.0 or greater.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.2 Understanding the Integration Architecture</h3>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 300\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"150\" width=\"200\" height=\"120\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dbe6fb\" stroke=\"#8ea9df\"/>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\" font-weight=\"700\">Eagle Eye Data Center</text>\n  <rect x=\"260\" y=\"150\" width=\"160\" height=\"120\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f2f3f6\" stroke=\"#9aa0ac\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,3\"/>\n  <text x=\"340\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\">EEN Bridge</text>\n  <text x=\"340\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"22\">&#128247;&#128247;&#128247;</text>\n  <text x=\"340\" y=\"255\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5b6270\">IP Cameras</text>\n  <rect x=\"470\" y=\"150\" width=\"150\" height=\"90\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#0b0f19\"/>\n  <text x=\"545\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\">AI Bridge</text>\n  <line x1=\"420\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"470\" y2=\"195\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" marker-end=\"url(#arre)\"/>\n  <text x=\"440\" y=\"185\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5b6270\">RTSP</text>\n  <line x1=\"220\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"260\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"470\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#2653d6\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" marker-end=\"url(#arre)\"/>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"163\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#2653d6\">HTTPS &ndash; Events (LPR, Loitering, Intrusion ...)</text>\n  <rect x=\"640\" y=\"30\" width=\"120\" height=\"70\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dcefe0\" stroke=\"#7fbf95\"/>\n  <text x=\"700\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#20603a\">AILN Cloud</text>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"640\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,3\" marker-end=\"url(#arre)\"/>\n  <text x=\"450\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5b6270\">Event Notification</text>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"22\">&#128241;</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5b6270\">AILN Mobile App</text>\n  <line x1=\"640\" y1=\"55\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"35\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#arre)\"/>\n  <text x=\"380\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5b6270\">Event Push</text>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arre\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f9c\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>The EEN Bridge streams video to AI Bridge; AI Bridge analyzes it and sends metadata/events back to the EEN cloud</figcaption>\n</div>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>The EEN Bridge, registered in the Eagle Eye Networks Cloud, transmits the video stream to the AI Bridge.</li>\n<li>The AI Bridge analyzes the received video stream using its AI apps.</li>\n<li>The AI Bridge sends metadata and events (via HTTPS) to the Eagle Eye Networks cloud through the EEN action handler.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>2. Eagle Eye Networks (EEN) Configuration</h2>\n<p>Before connecting the EEN Bridge to the AI Bridge, you must first register the EEN Bridge in your EEN account and configure several settings on the EEN platform.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.1 Registering EEN Bridge User Accounts</h3>\n<p>User account registration is required to connect to the EEN Bridge from the AI Bridge and send events to cameras. From the left sidebar, select <strong>Users</strong>, then click <strong>Add User</strong>. Enter the required account information &mdash; the email must be valid, since email verification is required &mdash; then click <strong>Next</strong>.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">If using an already registered email, you may use the format <code>abc+test@gmail.com</code>. Verification emails will go to <code>abc@gmail.com</code> without the suffix.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Select <strong>Administrator</strong> for permissions, then click <strong>Next</strong>. On the Access tab, click <strong>Next</strong> again. On the Cameras tab, set camera access permissions for the account, then click <strong>Save</strong>.</p>\n<p>Upon completion, a password setup email is sent to the registered address &mdash; set your password following the email instructions. After setting your password, check Users to confirm the status shows <strong>Active</strong>.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.2 Configuring QL Stream on the EEN Bridge</h3>\n<p>QL Stream must be enabled on the EEN Bridge. This allows the AI Bridge to fetch RTSP URLs for the cameras connected to that EEN Bridge. Click the settings button on the EEN Bridge, then under the <strong>Local Display</strong> tab, enable <strong>QL Stream (RTSP)</strong> &mdash; enabling <strong>QL Stream Auth</strong> is also recommended for enhanced security.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Enabling QL Stream (RTSP) allows full-resolution camera streaming over the local network.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>3. AI Bridge Configuration</h2>\n<p>This section describes how to fetch RTSP streams from your EEN Cloud-registered cameras into the AI Bridge, and how to configure action handlers in the AI Bridge.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.1 Registering Camera Streams</h3>\n<p>Navigate to <strong>VIDEO &gt; Video Input &gt; Video Stream</strong> from the left sidebar, then click <strong>Search Cameras</strong>. Select <strong>Eagle Eyes Network</strong> under Search Method, then click <strong>Login</strong> and sign in with the account registered in section 2.1. Click <strong>Device Search</strong>, then select <strong>View</strong> on the Bridge containing the desired camera. Select the channel for mapping, then click <strong>Submit</strong>.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.2 Configuring Action Handlers</h3>\n<p>Action handlers must be configured in the AI Bridge so it can send event notifications (e.g. LPR Detection) to the Eagle Eye Networks cloud, associated with the respective cameras. This example uses LPR Detection.</p>\n<p>AIBridge provides over 50 AI applications for various use cases &mdash; see the full app list at the <a href=\"https://indoai.com/goods/catalog?page=1&searchMode=catalog&category=c0006&per=40&sorting=ranking&filter_display=lattice&code=0006\">catalog link</a>.</p>\n<p>Click <strong>Configure AI App</strong> next to the registered Video Stream, select <strong>LPR-Europe</strong>, then click <strong>Add Rule</strong> and add an Event Setting. Configure the detection region and click <strong>Apply</strong>.</p>\n<p>Click <strong>Action Setting Add</strong>, select <strong>Eagle Eye Networks</strong> for Action Type, then click <strong>Eagle Eye Networks Action Add</strong>. Click <strong>Edit</strong> next to EEN Login, then click <strong>Login</strong> and sign in with the account registered in section 2.1. Click <strong>Mapping</strong> to confirm the camera mapping is correct &mdash; this is determined automatically from the stream registered in section 3.1 &mdash; then click <strong>Submit</strong>.</p>\n<p>Configure the message sent with events using String Construction and event tokens, then click <strong>Test</strong>. If an error appears, recheck your account details. If the test passes, click <strong>Apply</strong>, confirm the dialog, check the action's checkbox, click <strong>Apply</strong> again, then <strong>Submit</strong> and confirm.</p>\n\n<h2>4. Demo</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">4.1 Live</h3>\n<p>Live footage from cameras connected via the EEN Bridge can be viewed directly within the AI Bridge interface after stream registration.</p>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">4.2 Event</h3>\n<p>Triggered action handler events can be viewed in the EEN website timeline. In the EEN website, navigate to <strong>Layouts</strong>, and for the relevant camera click the Events button to view its event timeline. For LPR Detection, events appear as green markers on the timeline, and footage can be replayed from the exact event time.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Timeline colors vary per event type &mdash; refer to EEN documentation for details.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>5. FAQ</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">5.1 Mismatched Event Times on the EEN Timeline</h3>\n<p>If event times displayed in EEN don't match the AI Bridge, synchronize using NTP Time Sync on the AI Bridge (<strong>System &gt; Date / Time &gt; Network Time Server Setup</strong>).</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">5.2 Adding Annotated Videos with Bounding Boxes or Event Zones to EEN</h3>\n<p>AI Bridge provides annotated video by overlaying event information (bounding boxes, zones, widgets) on the original stream. This RTSP stream can be registered in EEN so the video can be viewed directly within the EEN platform.</p>\n<p>AI Bridge also offers a <strong>Dynamic View</strong> feature: register a single RTSP stream in EEN that automatically switches to display the channel where an event is detected, letting you monitor alarms across multiple channels through one registered stream.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Since EEN only supports RTSP streams over port 554, change the RTSP Port to 554 under <strong>AI Bridge &gt; Service Port</strong>, then click Apply.</li>\n<li>Configure the On-Screen Display (OSD) settings under <strong>VIDEO &gt; Display &gt; OSD</strong> to control what annotations are overlaid (Zone, Bounding Box, Info Widget, Event Widget).</li>\n<li>In EEN, under <strong>Account Settings &gt; Camera</strong>, check <strong>Enable RTSP cameras</strong> and save changes.</li>\n<li>An add icon appears under Available Devices on the dashboard &mdash; click it, disable Dual Stream, enter the RTSP address (e.g. <code>192.168.77.183</code> / <code>live/ch1</code>), and enter the AI Bridge login details, then click <strong>Add Camera</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;\">Dynamic View RTSP stream URL example: <code>rtsp://[AI Bridge IP address]/live/dynamicview</code></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">For RTSP URL <code>rtsp://192.168.77.183/live/ch1</code>, enter IP as <code>192.168.77.183</code> and Video Resource URL as <code>live/ch1</code>.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Once registered, the AI Bridge annotated stream can be viewed in EEN either from the Actions column for that camera, or by selecting it within the Layouts tab.</p>\n\n<h2>6. Revision History</h2>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>v1.00 Initial document creation.</li>\n</ul>";
